        <div class="section-block">
            <h2>Relevant Projects</h2>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="row">
                    <h3>Annotator-Aware Two-Stage Pipeline Tweets Sexism Detection</h3>
                </div>
                <ul class="details">
                    <li>Empirically evaluated three sexism-detection systems (fine-tuned Transformer fusion; zero-shot AR & diffusion LLMs) using a unified two-stage bilingual-fusion pipeline with annotator demographics.</li>
                    <li>Paper published. Joy Chrissetyo Prajogo, Lung-Hao Lee, and Hsien-I Lin (2025). NYCU-NLP at EXIST 2025: An Empirical Study of Annotator-Aware Two-Stage Pipeline for Sexism Detection in Tweets. In Proceedings of the Working Notes of CLEF 2025 - Conference and Labs of the Evaluation Forum, Madrid, Spain, 9-12 September 2025, vol. 4038, pp. 2119-2132.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="row">
                    <h3>CycleGAN-Based Metallic Surface Defect Synthetic Image Data Generation</h3>
                </div>
                <ul class="details">
                    <li>Adapted CycleGAN to generate synthetic metallic surface defect images to diversify detection training data, now validating impact within an AOI pipeline.</li>
                    <li>Paper published. S. Sanjaya, H. -I. Lin and J. Prajogo, "CycleGAN-Based Synthetic Data Generation and Automatic Image Annotation for Metallic Surface Defect Detection," 2025 13th International Conference on Control, Mechatronics and Automation (ICCMA), Paris, France, 2025, pp. 528-533, doi: 10.1109/ICCMA67641.2025.11369560.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="row">
                    <h3>Robotic Generative AI 3-Cup and Ball Game</h3>
                </div>
                <ul class="details">
                    <li>Built the vision system for a Generative-AI 3-Cup-and-Ball robot demo using YOLOv7 + SORT and custom in-cup ball tracking.</li>
                    <li>Paper published. N. Khoirurizka, J. C. Prajogo, S. Perkins, C. -H. Kuo and H. -I. Lin, A Case of Cups and a Ball: Utilizing Generative Artificial Intelligence for Human-robotic Collaboration in Task Execution, 2024 International Automatic Control Conference (CACS), Taoyuan, Taiwan, 2024, pp. 1-6, doi: 10.1109/CACS63404.2024.10773301.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

